    "body": "## Problem\r\n\r\nRepro:\r\n\r\n`q:` to open the cmdwin, then:\r\n\r\n```vim\r\n:set nowinfixbuf\r\n:enew\r\n```\r\n\r\nNow nvim thinks the cmdwin is open when it isn't, this causes problems with `:messages` rendering, `:chist`, etc\r\n\r\nOr for a more obvious bug, then type:\r\n\r\n```vim\r\n:tabedit\r\n:tabonly\r\n```\r\nSo there's no possibility the cmdwin is open or sharing any open buffer.\r\n\r\nBut, `q:` --> `E1292: Command-line window is already open`\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\n\r\nHandle the cmdwin changing to other buffers",
    "closed_at": null,
